.TH "RECORD\-IMAGE\-PROJECT\.PY" "" "June 2026" ""
.SH "NAME"
\fBrecord\-image\-project\.py\fR
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
\fBrecord\-image\-project\.py\fR
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
\fBrecord\-image\-project\.py\fR queries the RECORD provenance database and produces a Graphviz DOT file visualising the project\-level metadata graph\. It connects to the database via the \fBrecord\fR library, calls \fBrecord\.draw_graph\fR with a fixed set of entity types and their label fields, and writes the result to \fBproject\.dot\fR in the current working directory\.
.P
The graph includes the following entity types, labelled by the specified field:
.TS
allbox;
l l.
Entity type	Label field
\fBPersons\fR	\fBID_PERSON\fR
\fBProjects\fR	\fBID_PROJECT\fR
\fBApplications\fR	\fBname\fR
\fBDocumentation\fR	\fBID_DOCUMENTATION\fR
\fBBoxes\fR	\fBID_BOX\fR
.TE
.P
The resulting \fBproject\.dot\fR file can be rendered to an image using Graphviz, for example with \fBdot \-Tpng project\.dot \-o project\.png\fR\.
.SH "OPTIONS"
This script accepts no options or arguments\. The entity types, label fields, and output path are all hard\-coded\.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
Returns 0 on success\.
.P
Returns non\-zero if:
.IP "\(bu" 4
the \fBrecord\fR library cannot be imported from \fBlib/\fR; or
.IP "\(bu" 4
a database connection or query error occurs\.
.IP "" 0
.SH "ENVIRONMENT"
The script inherits all database connection environment variables from the \fBrecord\fR library\. Refer to \fBrecord\.py\fR for the full list, including:
.TP
\fBRECORD_DBTYPE\fR
Selects the database backend\. One of \fBsqlite3\fR, \fBpostgres\fR, or \fBgremlin\fR\.
.TP
\fBRECORD_DBFILE\fR
Path to the SQLite database file\. Used when \fBRECORD_DBTYPE\fR is \fBsqlite3\fR\.
.TP
\fBRECORD_DBUSER\fR
PostgreSQL username\. Used when \fBRECORD_DBTYPE\fR is \fBpostgres\fR\.
.TP
\fBRECORD_DBNAME\fR
PostgreSQL database name\. Used when \fBRECORD_DBTYPE\fR is \fBpostgres\fR\.
.TP
\fBRECORD_POSTGRES_HOST\fR
PostgreSQL hostname\.
.TP
\fBRECORD_POSTGRES_PORT\fR
PostgreSQL port number\.
.TP
\fBRECORD_POSTGRES_PASSWORD\fR
PostgreSQL password\. Required when \fBRECORD_DBTYPE\fR is \fBpostgres\fR\.
.TP
\fBRECORD_GREMLIN_HOST\fR
WebSocket URL of the Gremlin server\.
.TP
\fBRECORD_GREMLIN_TIMEOUT\fR
Per\-query evaluation timeout in milliseconds\.
.TP
\fBRECORD_DEBUG\fR
When set, enables verbose diagnostic output to standard error\.
.SH "RETURN VALUE"
Writes the Graphviz DOT representation of the project metadata graph to \fBproject\.dot\fR in the current working directory\. Any existing \fBproject\.dot\fR file will be overwritten without warning\.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
Generate the project graph and render it to PNG:
.IP "" 4
.nf
record\-image\-project\.py
dot \-Tpng project\.dot \-o project\.png
.fi
.IP "" 0
.P
Generate and render to SVG for use in documentation:
.IP "" 4
.nf
record\-image\-project\.py
dot \-Tsvg project\.dot \-o project\.svg
.fi
.IP "" 0
.SH "FILES"
.TP
\fBlib/record\.py\fR
The RECORD provenance library\. Must be importable as \fBrecord\fR; the script appends \fBlib\fR to \fBsys\.path\fR before importing, so \fBrecord\.py\fR must be present in a \fBlib/\fR subdirectory relative to the working directory\.
.TP
\fBproject\.dot\fR
Output Graphviz DOT file written to the current working directory\. Overwritten on each run without warning\.
